  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "In certain cases, the dcDates table is not updated when the DC datastream is updated.  The dcDates table is populated IF a dc:date can be parsed as a date.  This supported the range queries of fieldsearch.  In the event that the dcDates table has an entry for a given object (the DC date could be parsed), then the object is modified so that the DC date is not parsable, the old value is left in the dcDates table.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The expected behavior is that, if the new dc:date cannot be parsed, the old date would be removed from the dcDates table on modify, as this is supposed to represent the most current version's date.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
